      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, yes, this is a good observation.\n\nThere is a C++ wrapper that could be moved to unique_fd. However, there will always be a C version of this function that this doesn\u0027t apply to.\n\nAn alternative approach would be for jniCreateFileDescriptor to simply create an invalid descriptor and rely on a subsequent call to jniSetFileDescriptor. This is what it does internally anyway. This would make some of the awkward initializations we have in native code a bit easier, e.g. some folks initialize and array of file descriptors and that might end up a bit cleaner.\n\nI lean towards the latter as it\u0027s consistent between the C and C++ APIs. WDYT?",
